P96 driver development headers, release 3.6.0

These three headers are copied unchanged from the P96 development files
as kept in https://github.com/mheyer32/p96drivers/tree/master/Picasso96Develop
Snapshot: e6fd03e87486fd3dc4f5ca41934a843b7911d0a1

Sources:
  PrivateInclude/boardinfo.h      P96 Driver Development Files (P96CardDevelop)
  PrivateInclude/settings.h       P96 Driver Development Files (P96CardDevelop)
  Include/libraries/Picasso96.h   P96 Development Files (P96Develop)

Both archives are by Individual Computers (Jens Schoenfeld), uploaded to
Aminet by Thomas Richter (dev/misc/P96CardDevelop.lha and
dev/misc/P96Develop.lha); the headers' original authors are Alexander
Kneer and Tobias Abt. Their readmes, included here as
P96CardDevelop.readme and P96Develop.readme, say: "This archive is freely
distributable under CC-BY conditions, that is, it can be copied provided
you attribute its source correctly." Licence:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The original copyright line in Picasso96.h is kept as it was. These
headers describe the driver interface; no P96 implementation or card-driver
binary is included in PrismRTG.

Interface documentation:
https://wiki.icomp.de/wiki/P96_Driver_Development
